00:48:13,240 --> 00:48:20,280
 is for like loan. So, see that there are multiple data points let us say and here we are plotting

404
00:48:20,280 --> 00:48:28,880
 age as the X axis and the loan amount as the Y axis and as you see that with increasing

405
00:48:28,880 --> 00:48:38,000
 age and increasing loan amount there are a lot of default. So, and there are non-default

406
00:48:38,000 --> 00:48:45,360
 when the age is lower or the loan amount is lower. Now, a new data point comes so we actually

407
00:48:45,360 --> 00:48:52,800
 look at the neighbors the nearest neighbors and see what kind of labels they have. Now,

408
00:48:52,800 --> 00:48:58,840
 in this case if your algorithm is just majority voting it will lead to a deadlock because here

409
00:48:58,840 --> 00:49:06,280
 there is no solution, but if your result is based on weighted voting then you look at

410
00:49:06,280 --> 00:49:14,440
 whether this particular person has age or loan amount which is closer to the default

411
00:49:14,440 --> 00:49:21,720
 ones or the non-default ones. And depending on that the classifier will predict whether

412
00:49:21,720 --> 00:49:31,640
 this person is going to default or not. Now, again like as we said that if K is too small

413
00:49:31,640 --> 00:49:38,560
 then it will be like very noisy and it will be prone to a sensitive to noise points.

414
00:49:38,560 --> 00:49:44,640
 On the other hand if K is very large then you the neighborhood may actually cover almost

415
00:49:44,640 --> 00:49:51,560
 all the data points. So, in that case it will not be like very useful. So, how to choose

416
00:49:51,560 --> 00:49:58,960
 the value of K? Now, not only this particular scenario in a lot of other scenarios, often

417
00:49:58,960 --> 00:50:06,520
 time we have to pick some value of some parameters which we also call as hyper parameters. For

418
00:50:06,520 --> 00:50:12,720
 example, K is an hyper parameter in case of K nearest neighbor or for example, the kind

419
00:50:12,720 --> 00:50:18,480
 of distance function we are using the choice of the distance to use this is also another

420
00:50:18,480 --> 00:50:24,680
 choice which we will have to make. Now, in general whenever we have to choose hyper parameter

421
00:50:24,680 --> 00:50:31,760
 values, we choose the one which likely to give the best performance on the test data.

422
00:50:31,760 --> 00:50:39,320
 Now, in reality you do not know the test data, you are just given the training data. So,

423
00:50:39,320 --> 00:50:43,800
 you are just using the training data to train your model and test data will come only in

424
00:50:43,800 --> 00:50:49,760
 the real world like when you are having to deploy your model to work in the real world.

425
00:50:49,760 --> 00:50:57,740
 So, there is no way while you are developing the model you know the test. So, there is

426
00:50:57,740 --> 00:51:04,320
 a process by which we do this and this is called cross validation. So, let us just assume

427
00:51:04,320 --> 00:51:08,560
 that we are talking about binary classification just between like class 1 and class 2. In

428
00:51:08,560 --> 00:51:15,400
 this case let us say it is green or red. So, your test data is something like this like

429
00:51:15,400 --> 00:51:20,880
 where you have both values of class 1, both values of class 2. So, this is your training

430
00:51:20,880 --> 00:51:27,020
 data. Now, in test data these labels are something which you do not know like whether

431
00:51:27,020 --> 00:51:33,280
 a test data is actually green or actually red and there is no picking. So, that means

432
00:51:33,280 --> 00:51:38,640
 that you when you are building the model you cannot really look at the test data and then

433
00:51:38,640 --> 00:51:43,280
 decide oh this is working fine for the test data and we should try that.

434
00:51:43,280 --> 00:51:50,120
 So, to avoid that we actually do one thing, we take the training data, we divide the training

435
00:51:50,120 --> 00:51:57,360
 data into two parts. In one we actually take that as an actual training set, the other

436
00:51:57,360 --> 00:52:03,320
 data part we keep it separate we call them as validation set. So, this validation set

437
00:52:03,320 --> 00:52:11,440
 is very important because this actually helps us, this helps us determine what is the ideal

438
00:52:11,440 --> 00:52:20,440
 parameter value for a particular hyper parameter. So, what we do is we randomly split the original

439
00:52:20,440 --> 00:52:26,680
 data into actual training data set and validation set. We by using the actual training set we

440
00:52:26,680 --> 00:52:31,760
 train several times each time with a different value of the hyper parameter and then we pick

441
00:52:31,760 --> 00:52:36,040
 the hyper parameter value that gives the best accuracy on the validation set.

442
00:52:36,040 --> 00:52:43,120
 So, validation set in some sense kind of acts as a proxy of the test set where we do not

443
00:52:43,120 --> 00:52:48,880
 look at the final test set, but we look at the validation set to validate our choice

444
00:52:48,880 --> 00:53:02,120
 of hyper parameter. So, just to summarize, so to summarize essentially KNN classifiers

445
00:53:02,120 --> 00:53:08,080
 are also called lazy learners because they do not build a model upfront, but rather on

446
00:53:08,080 --> 00:53:15,400
 the test time they try to pick up or try to look at which are the data points which are

447
00:53:15,400 --> 00:53:21,000
 closer to the current test data point and based on that closer neighborhood selection

448
00:53:21,000 --> 00:53:28,760
 we tend to apply a particular level which is majority over the neighborhood set.

449
00:53:28,760 --> 00:53:35,220
 Now this is different from learners which we call as eager learners such as decision

450
00:53:35,220 --> 00:53:44,240
 tree or rule based system where the rules are built explicitly. So, in if you compare

451
00:53:44,240 --> 00:53:49,240
 a model which has already been trained and then based on that you are making a decision

452
00:53:49,240 --> 00:53:56,440
 versus a system like KN nearest neighbor where a test time a lot of compute needs to happen.

453
00:53:56,440 --> 00:54:06,580
 Oftentimes KNN is much more expensive to classify unknown records. So, with this let us take

454
00:54:06,580 --> 00:54:15,840
 a small break and then let us come back here with let us continue our discussion on supervised

455
00:54:15,840 --> 00:54:20,760
 learning, but we will take up a new classifier model which is called support vector machine

456
00:54:20,760 --> 00:54:35,340
 or SVM. So, see you soon.

